Z||000000||martin1875||12-09-2000||08:55 PM||||i bought a wrecked 86 se 2.8 .trided starting engine, started up and ran real rough then back fireded won't start now. turned engine over to tdc using wide timing mark. rotor points to number two contact on the dirtributer cap. turned engine over 180 degrees the rotor points to the number five contact on the distributer cap. my guess is the timing chain has jumped a couple of teeth.can anyone help me with this problem||||reg||9
Z||000001||terryk||12-10-2000||01:25 AM||||The only sure way to check is to remove the valve cover on the 1-3-5 bank, dial the crank up to TDC and check the #1 valves for being closed. Jumping a tooth like that is rare even with a severely worn chain. <P>I assume you checked the firing order? Sounds more like the timing is off. Bring the engine to TDC and crank the dist to match #1 on the dist. If it starts, ground the ALDL A-&gt;B and set the timing to 10 degrees.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||martin1875||12-10-2000||02:17 PM||||i pulled the 1# and the 2# spark plugs. tuned engine over to tdc using the wide timing mark. rotor still points to the number 2# and 5# contacs on the disrtibuter cap. is there a timing mark and a tdc mark.what are the other slots on the balencer.engine turns over slower than it should even with a good battery and charger||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||12-10-2000||02:47 PM||||The rotor has got to be pointing to the #1 plug wire when at tdc.The wires can be moved so that they are at the right location, or , the dist may be installed off by a tooth or two.It doesn't matter what location the plug wires are at as long as they are in time , and in the correct firing order.||||reg||6
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||12-10-2000||03:52 PM||||Make sure that the mark your using is the WIDEST of the three!||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||12-10-2000||06:39 PM||||Remove the cap and rotate the crank. Does the distributor rotate? If not, you don't have a jumped timing chain, you have a broken chain.||||reg||1
Z||000006||martin1875||12-10-2000||08:25 PM||||thanks for all the help. moved the wires on the cap to match the rotor,fired right up on the first try. guess someone else has intstalled the distributer off buy a few degrees.now iam on to my next problem water in the oil. when i brought the car home i changed the oil and there was no water in it.now there is.maybe its there because of the length of time it sat with out runing.i ll change the oil again and see what happens||||reg||1
